830-4qojoz --json` (CR2 accepted, tree the tree recorded in .task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md, the 219okr revision checkpointed) and `task-board worktree integrating`, then `git fetch origin` and record what origin/main actually is; if it moved past the CR base, say so explicitly in the outcome — the reparent is the integrate command's job, not yours. (2) Run `task-board worktree integrate STORY-260830-4qojoz --cr TASK-260830-19bjfj --revision 2 --commit-time \"$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\"` (version_control.confirm is enabled, so the explicit RFC3339 commit time is required; use the current real UTC time, never backdate). This lands one squash commit carrying the accepted Story tree on local main plus one board-only commit \"Record STORY-260830-4qojoz board state\", both SSH-signed as Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>. NOTE: unlike most leaves, this candidate DOES change `task-board.config.json` — it adds the new bounded fuzz commands this leaf ships. That is an exact reviewed change of the configured validation source and is expected; do not revert it and do not \"fix\" the config by hand. If integrate refuses for any reason — including `integration_base_moved` or `validation_suite_changed` — run `task-board worktree transaction show STORY-260830-4qojoz`, record the exact typed refusal and transaction state verbatim in the task notes and in the outcome, and stop immediately; the recovery cycle is the orchestrator's call, never yours. (3) Verify: `git verify-commit` on both new commits; `git rev-parse <story commit>^{tree}` and, if it differs from the tree recorded in .task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md, produce the exact `git diff the tree recorded in .task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md <story commit>^{tree}` and account for every file in it (a reparent onto an advanced trunk legitimately carries the trunk delta and nothing