{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3cd","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1dd-6f7d-7c42-8699-978ff86891e1"},"sequence":65,"recorded_at":1780531400000125,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b1dd-a572-7801-84d5-adec69d9f1d1"},"task_id":"01a0b1dd-a572-7801-84d5-adec69d9f1d1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b1dd-a572-7801-84d5-adec69d9f1d1","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_reviewer-cr2.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 2 of TASK-260830-19bjfj (fuzz-rpc-operations-and-version-skew, the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-4qojoz mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation — story_final, so the Change Request carries the WHOLE Story: story_final on trunk base 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91 with the checkpointed predecessor commits 544c389  on the Story branch (tip 544c389e019af28dc675b64b6404065eefffa766), published by RUN-260917-a36df8 on muse-spark max, 20 changed paths in the whole-Story patch, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-19bjfj_change-request_rev2.patch / _rev2-validation.log). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-19bjfj_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-19bjfj_results.md, TASK-260830-19bjfj_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-19bjfj_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the predecessor leaf's accepted evidence (TASK-260830-219okr_results.md and its verdict TASK-260830-219okr_review-verdict-rev4.md, accepted by RUN-260917-b1ebcb), the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md Sections 11.2-11.3 and 17.1-17.4 (byte-identical to the v0.6.0 text in these sections; the v0.7.0 adoption landed as trunk commit 32ee605). The landed owners are internal/rpcwire (envelope, framing, majors 2-5, the existing FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes gate), internal/hostchannel (RPC 5 endpoint admission) and internal/meshneg (this Story's first leaf).\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments. (0) REWORK VERIFICATION FIRST — revision 1 was routed CHANGES REQUESTED by RUN-260917-81d7ae, which found the technical body STRONG (the three inherited advisories genuinely closed, every producer mutant reproducing, its own 38 narrowing plants dying twice, all three fuzz targets failing on their controls, and the producer's reported 23-of-29 AC ratio equal to its own measurement) and blocked acceptance on the story-close half: the candidate was built on the stale base 888ae3d and bound the NO-LONGER-ADOPTED internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json, so `git apply --check` of the patch on trunk failed on five paths and the registry work, the digest re-pin, the tracecheck ratios, the README coverage subsection and the LOGBOOK ratios all described a registry the adopted tree does not read. Plus P2-1 (clause 11.3#18 bound to tests that drive no digest-identity array — an invented binding that inflates the measured ratio) and eight P3 instrument defects. Read TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz, and grade every one of those findings on your own executed evidence. The registry half is where a plausible-looking rework can still be wrong, so check it directly: the bindings must live in ownership.v0.7.0.json, every clause `line` coordinate must be RE-MEASURED against SPEC.v0.7.0.md (they moved between releases — verify them yourself rather than trusting either the producer's or the previous reviewer's numbers), reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 must be re-derived from the registry as it stands in THIS candidate (recompute it and compare), the README subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on this tree AND pass the landed readme_coverage_pin_test.go with its closed spelled-number map, and any binding that survived must name a clause an executed test actually drives. Re-run the reviewer plants R9, J1 and the fuzz-oracle plants from the evidence archive against the new tree and watch them die. IMPORTANT — this revision MODIFIES tests that trunk landed with the v0.7.0 adoption: `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/readme_coverage_pin_test.go` and `internal/traceability/registry_rederivation_test.go`. Extending the pin test's closed spelled-number map is legitimate when the new figures need a word it lacks, and the rework brief allowed exactly that — but a pin test is also the easiest thing to 'fix' by loosening. Diff both files against `git show 2fc6d50:<path>` and judge every hunk: a widened tolerance, a dropped assertion, a regex made permissive, a number map turned open-ended or a skipped case is a P1 regardless of how green the suite is. The test must still fail if the README figures and the tracecheck output disagree — prove that by perturbing one figure and watching it redden. Then proceed to your own independent review of the whole revision: (1) Spec fidelity — extract the Section 11.3 operation table, the closed embedded types (Namespace, LeaseExpectation, LeaseHead, GroupMemberExpectation, WorkspaceGroupExpectation, MaterializationKind, MaterializationIntent) and the Section 11.2 framing rules from the pinned text YOURSELF and diff them against the candidate: exact member sets, every bound at both edges and one step outside, `initiator_host_id` on every mutation body, an exact lease expectation on every session mutation, and both revalidated immediately before the mutation. Any operation the producer lists as a STATED BOUND must be checked against the code: a bound is honest only if the body genuinely is not parsed anywhere. (2) Fuzz targets are the deliverable here, so attack the instruments, not only the production code: for each new target confirm it actually reaches the body parser rather than the envelope, plant a body it must reject and prove the target FAILS on it (a fuzz target that cannot fail is not evidence), check the corpus is seeded and deterministic, and confirm the new task-board.config.json commands are bounded (`-fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`) and were really executed — Change Request construction runs the CONTROL ROOT's suite, so the new commands are NOT in the constructed evidence and the producer must have run them by hand with attached raw logs. (3) Section 17 skew — drive it, do not read it: a namespaced `extensions` entry admitted and the same data at top level refused; a peer offering only a higher major, only a lower major, an empty set, a duplicate, an unsorted array and an out-of-range count each refusing through meshneg with no coerced selection; a 2.0.0 peer rejecting major 1; and a peer attempting to negotiate the embedded Structured Error version refused (RPC 2 binds Error 1.0.0, RPC 4/5 bind 1.3.0, never negotiated separately). (4) Replay and lost response — a mismatched `request_id` echo refuses, a duplicate `request_id` with an identical body replays the same result, a duplicate with a CHANGED body is `idempotency_mismatch`, `materialize.status` recovers the exact durable phase after a lost response, and a blind retry after a committed effect never doubles it. (5) Framing — 8388608 accepted and 8388609 refused, an embedded newline, a truncated line, valid JSON that is not an object, unpadded base64url accepted while padded/standard-alphabet is refused, and `max_object_bytes` enforced independently of `max_line_bytes`. (6) STORY-CLOSE ITEMS, the part most likely to be wrong on a final leaf: the ownership registry edited must be `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json` (the adopted one — v0.6.0 is no longer adopted and editing it would be invisible), every binding must name a clause an executed test actually drives, `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` must be RE-DERIVED from the registry as it stands in the candidate (recompute it yourself and compare; a digest copied from another Story or left stale is a P1), `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` and the section-scoped runs must be green on the exact candidate tree with the ratios quoted verbatim in the results, the README \"Measured coverage of this repository\" subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on this tree (the landed `readme_coverage_pin_test.go` pins it — confirm the test is actually exercised and not bypassed), and the LOGBOOK entry must be newest-first and factually true. (7) Mutation — rerun the shipped harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, and plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on gates the producer did not mutate (one member check dropped, one bound widened by one, an unsorted array admitted, the pre-mutation revalidation skipped) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (8) Bounds and hygiene — the candidate must be byte-identical to trunk 2fc6d50 everywhere it is not this Story's scope (a refresh-candidate carries stale pre-refresh copies into the candidate and they read as reverts: check every path in `git diff --name-only <the CR base> 2fc6d50`), README and LOGBOOK edits purely additive on the NEW content, no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`, gofmt/vet clean, and the full 27-command suite green on the exact tree with command 5 (`-race`, 25m) and command 21 (`cataloggen -adopted -check`) recorded.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-19bjfj/ and delete candidate copies when done. Report the coverage ratio YOU measured against the acceptance table's real row count, not the producer's restated one. Attach TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md and TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-19bjfj, revision=2, evidence=TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named and a short \"Rework scope (for the producer)\" section at the end. Model: claude-opus-5 max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","final_result":true}}}
