{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1dd-6f7d-7c42-8699-978ff86891e1"},"sequence":67,"recorded_at":1780531400000129,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1dd99cc71bbb6a44d7e0994df03","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_rework-rev2.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES EVERY EARLIER PRECONDITION ON TASK-260830-19bjfj, including TASK-260830-19bjfj_producer.md. Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-19bjfj (fuzz-rpc-operations-and-version-skew, the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-4qojoz). Change Request revision 1 was reviewed by RUN-260917-81d7ae (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED. Read TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz before touching anything. The reviewer calls the technical body of your leaf STRONG and I agree: the three inherited advisories are genuinely closed, every mutant you shipped reproduces, the reviewer's own 38 narrowing plants die twice, all three fuzz targets fail on their controls, and the AC ratio you reported (23 of 29) is exactly the ratio the reviewer measured independently. Do not rewrite any of that. What blocks acceptance is the story-close half, and the root cause is an orchestration failure of mine, not a judgement error of yours: the v0.7.0 adoption landed on trunk while you were already running, and the TRUNK STATE paragraph was appended to your brief nine minutes after you started, so your run never saw it. Your results say \"v0.7.0 has not landed (internal/specdoc holds v0.6.0 only)\" — that was a true observation of your worktree and a false statement about trunk. This rework fixes that.\n3|P1-1 — rebase the story-close work onto the adopted registry. (a) Run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-19bjfj` FIRST. The Story branch carries one checkpoint commit (TASK-260830-219okr rev4), so use the checkpoint-bound `--replay-resolutions` path: copy the retained resolution-template.json header and add one entry per conflicted path with {\"checkpoint_oid\": <the ORIGINAL checkpoint OID recorded before the refresh>, \"path\": ..., \"sha256\": <hex of the full replacement>, \"content\": <base64>}, keeping LOGBOOK entries newest-first. (b) `git diff --name-only 888ae3d 2fc6d50` overlaps your candidate at exactly five paths — LOGBOOK.md, README.md, internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/main_test.go, internal/traceability/traceability.go, internal/traceability/traceability_test.go — and the reviewer measured that `git apply --check` of your patch on trunk fails on all five. After the refresh, reconcile every one of them against TRUNK's version (`git show 2fc6d50:<path>`): your edits go on top of the new content, never restoring the old bytes. traceability.go on trunk carries an 80-line v0.7.0 change including `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` — keep trunk's structure and change only the digest. (c) Move ALL registry work into `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`. The v0.6.0 registry is no longer adopted: trunk's tracecheck does not read it, so the six new acceptance cases and the four upgraded bindings you wrote are invisible there. (d) The clause `line` coordinates in your bindings are v0.6.0 line numbers and the same sentences sit elsewhere in SPEC.v0.7.0.md — RE-MEASURE every one of them yourself against the pinned v0.7.0 document (the verdict quotes the reviewer's measurements; treat them as a cross-check, never as input to copy). (e) RE-DERIVE `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` from the v0.7.0 registry as it stands in your candidate and show the derivation command and its output in the results. (f) Re-run `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` plus the section-scoped runs on the refreshed tree and quote the ratios verbatim. (g) The README \"Measured coverage of this repository\" subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on the refreshed tree — and note that trunk now ships `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/readme_coverage_pin_test.go`, which pins that subsection to the tool's own output through a CLOSED spelled-number map (two, four, five, six, seven, fifty-two, sixty-eight): if your new figures need a word that map does not contain, extend the map deliberately in the same change and say so. (h) Recompute the LOGBOOK ratios on the refreshed tree.\n4|P2-1 — remove the invented binding. Clause 11.3#18 (\"Arrays with digest identities MUST be sorted bytewise and contain no duplicate\") is bound to `rpcwire-inventory-arrays`, but no production code in internal/rpcwire parses an array of digest identities: `decodeNamespaces` validates a sorted-unique array of vocabulary STRINGS and `validateRoots` reads one `root_id` per root. The clause is about object_ids / known_lease_record_ids / installed_object_ids / manifest_ids / VerifiedState.object_ids — all inside bodies you correctly list as opaque stated bounds. Drop the binding (11.3 stays unevidenced) or rebind it to a test that genuinely drives a digest-identity array, and carry the resulting change through the headline `clauses_discharged` figure, the README and the LOGBOOK. The producer brief said never to invent a binding for a clause no test drives; this is that.\n5|P3 — each item is named in the verdict with its plant and its log: P3-1 add a negative over an OPAQUE operation for a non-object body (`[]`, `null`, `\"x\"`, `42`, `{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}` -> ErrFrame) and let `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` feed non-object bodies — today both fuzzers normalise through `validObjectOrEmpty`, so neither can reach that arm, and the reviewer's plant survives twice; P3-2 drive a CHANGED body after a committed effect (`Create(moved)` after `setupPhase(t, store, PhaseCommitted)`) asserting the literal `idempotency_mismatch` and a single retained journal directory — the spec's rule carries no phase qualifier and only the staging member is measured; P3-3 the body fuzzer's oracle checks the member NAME SET only (a 15-byte nonce plant passes at 100x while the unit suite kills it) so either add an independent oracle for the hello bounds or state that bound explicitly, and add the missing hello-body-extra seed to `FuzzUnknownFields`; P3-4 make `encode-refuses-8388609` an exact edge witness or state the encode direction as subsumed by decode; P3-5 pin the refusal CLASS through `axerror.DecodeBound` in `TestErrorSchemaNotNegotiated` instead of asserting only non-nil; P3-6 assert the literal offer sets ([2 3 4], [5]) in the N2 rows rather than computing `wantLocal` from `meshneg.LocalMajors`; P3-7 make the nonce alphabet plant a CLASS narrowing (translate `+`/`/` to `-`/`_` before decoding) instead of admitting one fixture string; P3-8 attach the raw logs for the six validation commands your table reports as exit 0, and fix the matrix row 22 citation (the pre-hello lane is `hello_half_frame_close`, not `mid_request_close`).\n6|Procedure: after the refresh your base is 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. Re-run the FULL configured validation suite once on the refreshed tree (it is no longer 27 commands — your own leaf adds the bounded fuzz commands; command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs). Update TASK-260830-19bjfj_results.md with a finding-by-finding table (finding -> change -> the test that fails without it -> evidence path), update TASK-260830-19bjfj_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-19bjfj_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, no __pycache__), reset and re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-19bjfj --role developer` so revision 2 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 3.5 hours in. Report the ratio you MEASURE on the refreshed tree, not the one from rev1.\n7|PARTIAL-ATTEMPT RECOVERY: if a previous attempt of this run died to a provider idle timeout, the Story worktree still carries its partial edits — start with `git -C .temp/STORY-260830-4qojoz/worktree status --short` and `git diff`, state what you inherited, and verify it against this brief instead of assuming it is correct.\n8|Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 2.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1dd-6f7d-7c42-8699-978ff86891e1"},"sequence":68,"recorded_at":1780531400000131,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1dd9cc17347961350fdfecf6463","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_reviewer-cr2.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 2 of TASK-260830-19bjfj (fuzz-rpc-operations-and-version-skew, the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-4qojoz mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation — story_final, so the Change Request carries the WHOLE Story: story_final on trunk base 2fc6d5074058ab7970c87982deac50b3e3f5fd91 with the checkpointed predecessor commits 544c389  on the Story branch (tip 544c389e019af28dc675b64b6404065eefffa766), published by RUN-260917-a36df8 on muse-spark max, 20 changed paths in the whole-Story patch, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-19bjfj_change-request_rev2.patch / _rev2-validation.log). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-19bjfj_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-19bjfj_results.md, TASK-260830-19bjfj_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-19bjfj_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the predecessor leaf's accepted evidence (TASK-260830-219okr_results.md and its verdict TASK-260830-219okr_review-verdict-rev4.md, accepted by RUN-260917-b1ebcb), the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md Sections 11.2-11.3 and 17.1-17.4 (byte-identical to the v0.6.0 text in these sections; the v0.7.0 adoption landed as trunk commit 32ee605). The landed owners are internal/rpcwire (envelope, framing, majors 2-5, the existing FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes gate), internal/hostchannel (RPC 5 endpoint admission) and internal/meshneg (this Story's first leaf).\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments. (0) REWORK VERIFICATION FIRST — revision 1 was routed CHANGES REQUESTED by RUN-260917-81d7ae, which found the technical body STRONG (the three inherited advisories genuinely closed, every producer mutant reproducing, its own 38 narrowing plants dying twice, all three fuzz targets failing on their controls, and the producer's reported 23-of-29 AC ratio equal to its own measurement) and blocked acceptance on the story-close half: the candidate was built on the stale base 888ae3d and bound the NO-LONGER-ADOPTED internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json, so `git apply --check` of the patch on trunk failed on five paths and the registry work, the digest re-pin, the tracecheck ratios, the README coverage subsection and the LOGBOOK ratios all described a registry the adopted tree does not read. Plus P2-1 (clause 11.3#18 bound to tests that drive no digest-identity array — an invented binding that inflates the measured ratio) and eight P3 instrument defects. Read TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz, and grade every one of those findings on your own executed evidence. The registry half is where a plausible-looking rework can still be wrong, so check it directly: the bindings must live in ownership.v0.7.0.json, every clause `line` coordinate must be RE-MEASURED against SPEC.v0.7.0.md (they moved between releases — verify them yourself rather than trusting either the producer's or the previous reviewer's numbers), reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 must be re-derived from the registry as it stands in THIS candidate (recompute it and compare), the README subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on this tree AND pass the landed readme_coverage_pin_test.go with its closed spelled-number map, and any binding that survived must name a clause an executed test actually drives. Re-run the reviewer plants R9, J1 and the fuzz-oracle plants from the evidence archive against the new tree and watch them die. IMPORTANT — this revision MODIFIES tests that trunk landed with the v0.7.0 adoption: `internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck/readme_coverage_pin_test.go` and `internal/traceability/registry_rederivation_test.go`. Extending the pin test's closed spelled-number map is legitimate when the new figures need a word it lacks, and the rework brief allowed exactly that — but a pin test is also the easiest thing to 'fix' by loosening. Diff both files against `git show 2fc6d50:<path>` and judge every hunk: a widened tolerance, a dropped assertion, a regex made permissive, a number map turned open-ended or a skipped case is a P1 regardless of how green the suite is. The test must still fail if the README figures and the tracecheck output disagree — prove that by perturbing one figure and watching it redden. Then proceed to your own independent review of the whole revision: (1) Spec fidelity — extract the Section 11.3 operation table, the closed embedded types (Namespace, LeaseExpectation, LeaseHead, GroupMemberExpectation, WorkspaceGroupExpectation, MaterializationKind, MaterializationIntent) and the Section 11.2 framing rules from the pinned text YOURSELF and diff them against the candidate: exact member sets, every bound at both edges and one step outside, `initiator_host_id` on every mutation body, an exact lease expectation on every session mutation, and both revalidated immediately before the mutation. Any operation the producer lists as a STATED BOUND must be checked against the code: a bound is honest only if the body genuinely is not parsed anywhere. (2) Fuzz targets are the deliverable here, so attack the instruments, not only the production code: for each new target confirm it actually reaches the body parser rather than the envelope, plant a body it must reject and prove the target FAILS on it (a fuzz target that cannot fail is not evidence), check the corpus is seeded and deterministic, and confirm the new task-board.config.json commands are bounded (`-fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`) and were really executed — Change Request construction runs the CONTROL ROOT's suite, so the new commands are NOT in the constructed evidence and the producer must have run them by hand with attached raw logs. (3) Section 17 skew — drive it, do not read it: a namespaced `extensions` entry admitted and the same data at top level refused; a peer offering only a higher major, only a lower major, an empty set, a duplicate, an unsorted array and an out-of-range count each refusing through meshneg with no coerced selection; a 2.0.0 peer rejecting major 1; and a peer attempting to negotiate the embedded Structured Error version refused (RPC 2 binds Error 1.0.0, RPC 4/5 bind 1.3.0, never negotiated separately). (4) Replay and lost response — a mismatched `request_id` echo refuses, a duplicate `request_id` with an identical body replays the same result, a duplicate with a CHANGED body is `idempotency_mismatch`, `materialize.status` recovers the exact durable phase after a lost response, and a blind retry after a committed effect never doubles it. (5) Framing — 8388608 accepted and 8388609 refused, an embedded newline, a truncated line, valid JSON that is not an object, unpadded base64url accepted while padded/standard-alphabet is refused, and `max_object_bytes` enforced independently of `max_line_bytes`. (6) STORY-CLOSE ITEMS, the part most likely to be wrong on a final leaf: the ownership registry edited must be `internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json` (the adopted one — v0.6.0 is no longer adopted and editing it would be invisible), every binding must name a clause an executed test actually drives, `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` must be RE-DERIVED from the registry as it stands in the candidate (recompute it yourself and compare; a digest copied from another Story or left stale is a P1), `go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck` and the section-scoped runs must be green on the exact candidate tree with the ratios quoted verbatim in the results, the README \"Measured coverage of this repository\" subsection must equal what tracecheck prints on this tree (the landed `readme_coverage_pin_test.go` pins it — confirm the test is actually exercised and not bypassed), and the LOGBOOK entry must be newest-first and factually true. (7) Mutation — rerun the shipped harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, and plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on gates the producer did not mutate (one member check dropped, one bound widened by one, an unsorted array admitted, the pre-mutation revalidation skipped) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (8) Bounds and hygiene — the candidate must be byte-identical to trunk 2fc6d50 everywhere it is not this Story's scope (a refresh-candidate carries stale pre-refresh copies into the candidate and they read as reverts: check every path in `git diff --name-only <the CR base> 2fc6d50`), README and LOGBOOK edits purely additive on the NEW content, no `__pycache__`/`.pyc`, gofmt/vet clean, and the full 27-command suite green on the exact tree with command 5 (`-race`, 25m) and command 21 (`cataloggen -adopted -check`) recorded.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-19bjfj/ and delete candidate copies when done. Report the coverage ratio YOU measured against the acceptance table's real row count, not the producer's restated one. Attach TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md and TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-evidence-rev2.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-19bjfj, revision=2, evidence=TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named and a short \"Rework scope (for the producer)\" section at the end. Model: claude-opus-5 max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b1dd-6f7d-7c42-8699-978ff86891e1"},"sequence":69,"recorded_at":1780531400000133,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"0778112d-8f97-40f5-bc11-0d580ffc7c48"},"call_id":"call_01a0b1dda03e70a49bb9b23a3232bf9d","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_integration-rev2.md`.\n1|Integration-only continuation for the independently accepted Change Request revision 2 of TASK-260830-19bjfj, the FINAL leaf of STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation). Reviewer RUN-260917-e5ea66 accepted CR2 (story_final, candidate tree the tree recorded in .task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md; verdict TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md). This Story has TWO leaves: TASK-260830-219okr rev4 is already a signed checkpoint commit on the Story branch, and your revision is the whole-Story candidate on top of it — the squash therefore carries both. You are the bound producer-role integration run (developer role, implementer archetype, the same binding as the accepted revision); do NOT reimplement, edit, re-handoff or checkpoint anything, and do not touch the candidate bytes.\n2|\n3|Do exactly this from the control root /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager (trunk branch main; main's upstream is origin/main and MUST stay so — never use git push -u / --set-upstream from main): (1) verify the accepted record with `task-board worktree status STORY-260830-4qojoz --json` (CR2 accepted, tree the tree recorded in .task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md, the 219okr revision checkpointed) and `task-board worktree integrating`, then `git fetch origin` and record what origin/main actually is; if it moved past the CR base, say so explicitly in the outcome — the reparent is the integrate command's job, not yours. (2) Run `task-board worktree integrate STORY-260830-4qojoz --cr TASK-260830-19bjfj --revision 2 --commit-time \"$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)\"` (version_control.confirm is enabled, so the explicit RFC3339 commit time is required; use the current real UTC time, never backdate). This lands one squash commit carrying the accepted Story tree on local main plus one board-only commit \"Record STORY-260830-4qojoz board state\", both SSH-signed as Ivan Oparin <oparin@me.com>. NOTE: unlike most leaves, this candidate DOES change `task-board.config.json` — it adds the new bounded fuzz commands this leaf ships. That is an exact reviewed change of the configured validation source and is expected; do not revert it and do not \"fix\" the config by hand. If integrate refuses for any reason — including `integration_base_moved` or `validation_suite_changed` — run `task-board worktree transaction show STORY-260830-4qojoz`, record the exact typed refusal and transaction state verbatim in the task notes and in the outcome, and stop immediately; the recovery cycle is the orchestrator's call, never yours. (3) Verify: `git verify-commit` on both new commits; `git rev-parse <story commit>^{tree}` and, if it differs from the tree recorded in .task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md, produce the exact `git diff the tree recorded in .task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-19bjfj/TASK-260830-19bjfj_review-verdict-rev2.md <story commit>^{tree}` and account for every file in it (a reparent onto an advanced trunk legitimately carries the trunk delta and nothing else — an unexplained path is a stop); `git diff --stat origin/main..HEAD`; the story commit must touch zero `.task-board` paths. (4) Run the FULL configured validation suite from the NEW head's `task-board.config.json` (every command, in order, from the control root at the exact new head — the count is now higher than 27 because this leaf added fuzz commands; record every real exit). Command 5 is the race gate with `-timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs; the new fuzz commands are bounded (`-fuzztime=100x -parallel=1`). `git diff --check` inspects the ambient working tree, which carries live board dirt from concurrent runs: if it flags anything, run `git diff --check -- . ':!.task-board'` as well and report both, stating plainly which paths are board paths. (5) Push the two commits as a delivery branch WITHOUT changing main's upstream: `git push origin HEAD:refs/heads/delivery/STORY-260830-4qojoz-mesh-rpc`, then open a pull request against main with `gh pr create --head delivery/STORY-260830-4qojoz-mesh-rpc` (title \"STORY-260830-4qojoz: mesh RPC framing and negotiation (CR-TASK-260830-19bjfj-2 rev2)\", body stating the immutable binding: CR base, candidate tree, story commit, board commit, commit time, integrate exit, every gate exit including the new fuzz commands, and that the exact-head review and the plain fast-forward landing remain the orchestrator's acts; end the body with the attribution lines \"🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\" and \"https://claude.ai/code/session_012m24FtQAUcbuDSJn4KQr3E\"). (6) Do NOT push main and do NOT merge through GitHub. (7) Verify `git config branch.main.merge` is still `refs/heads/main` and record it. (8) Attach TASK-260830-19bjfj_integration-outcome-rev2.md (story/board commit OIDs, tree accounting, every gate exit, PR URL, upstream check) as a task-scoped outcome and exit. Model: muse-spark max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
