`section:11.3` binding byte-identical to trunk (unevidenced 0/27); `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` absent from the registry; re-adding an 11.3 clause is refused by the rederivation test (`acceptance cases moved …`) and by the digest | registry diff, `logs/registry-perturbation-01.log` |\\n| P3-1 opaque-body object gate | CLOSED | `TestOpaqueBodyMustBeObject` (5 lanes) exists; the producer's restructured probe `opaque-admits-nonobject-body` is KILLED ×2 in my rerun by `TestOpaqueBodyMustBeObject/{array,null,string,number}`; my R9b (same shape) KILLED ×2 by those lanes plus `FuzzClosedOperationBodies/seed#31–34`; `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` now feeds raw bytes and FAILS under the plant (`admitted request body is not a JSON object`, exit 1). Confirmed the producer's finding that rev1's R9 shape (`err != nil && op != \\\"health.get\\\"`) is vacuous: SURVIVED ×2 as an equivalent (the assigned `err` still propagates) | `reviewer-mutants/R9*`, `reviewer-fuzz/producer-p3-1-bodies-object-gate/` |\\n| P3-2 changed body after commit | CLOSED | `TestRPCChangedBodyAfterCommitRefusesMismatch` asserts the literal `idempotency_mismatch`, one retained journal dir and phase committed; rev1's J1 (both replay sites exempt `PhaseCommitted`) KILLED ×2 by exactly that test | `reviewer-mutants/J1-rev1-*` |\\n| P3-3 oracle bound + missing seed | CLOSED | Bound stated in the target's doc comment and README (\\\"member bounds and vocabularies are owned by the unit suite\\\"); `FuzzUnknownFields` carries the hello-body-extra seed (7 seeds measured) and now FAILS under the rev1 hello-body-extra class plant (exit 1) where it passed in rev1; the nonce-15 plant still passes the bodies target, which is the stated bound (the unit suite kills it: `nonce-short` KILLED ×2) | `reviewer-fuzz/rev1-*`, `logs/fuzz-seed-counts-01.log` |\\n| P3-4 encode edge | CLOSED | `encode-refuses-8388609` sizes the pad from a measured probe, asserts the admitted encoded line is exactly 8388608 bytes and that pad+1 refuses with `ErrFrame`; passes on the tree | `logs/pkg-tests-01.log` |\\n| P3-5 refusal class | CLOSED | Three refusal lanes assert `errors.Is(err, axerror.ErrVersionMismatch)`; producer probe `failure-binding-v2-admits-13` still KILLED ×2; my R6-analogue for RPC-4 is subsumed by the class assertion | `producer-harness-rerun/` |\\n| P3-6 production-derived expectations | CLOSED | `wantLocal` literal `[]int{2,3,4}` / `[]int{5}` in both N2 tests; no `LocalMajors` call remains in `adversarial_test.go` | source read |\\n| P3-7 class-level alphabet plant | CLOSED | `nonce-admits-standard-alphabet` now adds a second `RawStdEncoding.Strict()` arm (any canonical unpadded `+/` spelling ≥16 bytes) and is KILLED ×2 by `TestClosedBodyBoundsWitnessed/nonce-standard-alphabet-refused` alone | `producer-harness-rerun/rpcwire-run{1,2}/nonce-admits-standard-alphabet/` |\\n| P3-8 evidence hygiene / row 22 | PARTIALLY CLOSED (advisory A1) | Matrix row 22 now cites `hello_half_frame_close` (exists at `hostile_test.go:552`); `evidence/validation/*.log` are attached but all eight are 0 bytes with no exit line, and `evidence/mutants-rpcwire/` is the rev1-era harness output (40 rows: no `opaque-admits-nonobject-body` row, `nonce-admits-standard-alphabet/hello.go` is the old fixture plant) although the results cite both paths. The claims themselves are true — I re-ran every command and both harnesses with exits — but the attached artifact does not back them | `logs/validation-misc-0{1,2}.log`, `logs/producer-harness-rpcwire-run{1,2}.log` |\\n\\nInherited advisories N1/N2/N3 re-confirmed on the rev2 tree: 4 per-key N1 plants (`blob`, `session_record`, `session_annotation`, `terminal_backend_evidence`), S12 `Local = nil` (183 failing subtests) and S14 local major 1 — all KILLED ×2 (`reviewer-mutants-inherited/`).\\n\\n## (1) Spec fidelity\\n\\n- §11.3 table extracted by me: exactly 24 operations (`logs/spec-11.3-operations.txt`). Non-test Go census: only `hello` (rpcwire, hostchannel) and `inventory.roots` (rpcwire) are parsed; `materialize.{commit,rollback,status}` hits are `internal/provhost/protocol.go` = the provider protocol (`urn:ax:protocol:provider`, §7.2), not Mesh RPC; no `initiator_host_id`/`LeaseExpectation`/`GroupMemberExpectation`/`WorkspaceGroupExpectation`/`MaterializationKind|Intent` parser exists outside sessrepo's lease CAS type; hostchannel hands every post-hello request to a consumer `Handler` with no replay cache. The 22-operation bound, the embedded-type bound, the initiator/lease revalidation bound and the correlation-only `request_id` bound are honest.\\n- hello: 7 members (+`nonce_echo` on the response), each missing/wrong-type/extra refusing `ErrHello`; nonce 16 admitted / 15 refused; padded and standard-alphabet refused; contracts arrays 16 admitted / 17 refused; `max_line_bytes` 8388608 admitted / 8388607 refused with a generous object limit; `max_object_bytes` 5242880 admitted / 5242879 refused with a generous line limit (my V5 `<=` edge plant KILLED ×2 by `both-floors-admitted`). Namespace vocabularies per major equal §11.3/11.8/11.9 (`{6}`, `{7}`, `{8}`, `{8}`), near-miss spellings and future-major members refused.\\n- Registry clause bindings judged against the tests: 11.2#2 (forbidden contract keys) — trunk `TestHelloRefusals/error-key` + the exact 14-key gate; 11.2#3 (failure MUST omit body) — `TestHistoricalFailureBindings` asserts the encoded failure carries no `\\\"body\\\"` and `DecodeResponse` admits it, my V1 plant (failure envelope admitting a `body` member) KILLED ×2 by `TestUnknownFieldsRefusedEverywhere/failure-carries-body`; 11.2#4 (limit floors) — `TestClosedBodyBoundsWitnessed`; 17.1#1/#4/#5 — `TestNegotiateMatrix`, `TestNoMajorSelectedByCoercion` (the clause's MUST NOT is \\\"select a major by coercion\\\"; the minor sentence is non-normative prose), `TestMajor1Rejected*`; 17.4#4 — `TestPeerExposure` drives `Negotiate` and asserts the literal `directory_mesh_unsupported`/`terminal_backend_unavailable` exit-6 activations. Every bound clause is driven by an executed test.\\n\\n## (2) Fuzz targets — instruments attacked\\n\\n- Config diff = exactly the 3 new rows in the existing shape (`logs/validation-misc-01.log`); all three commands executed verbatim on the extract: exit 0 each (`reviewer-fuzz/config-*.log`). In-code seeds measured with `-run ^Fuzz…$`: bodies 38, nsvocab 22, unknownfields 7 (the \\\"gathering baseline\\\" figures in the logs are inflated by the shared GOCACHE fuzz cache, not by a committed corpus; no `testdata/fuzz` exists).\\n- Producer controls reproduced through `-overlay` with their own `planted.go` bytes: bodies FAIL, nsvocab FAIL, unknownfields FAIL, P3-1 object-gate FAIL, P3-3 hello-extra-on-unknownfields FAIL (`reviewer-fuzz/producer-*`).\\n- Reviewer measurements: nonce-15 PASS (stated bound); rev1 hello-body-extra class plant now FAIL; object gate exempting `session.status` PASS (unseeded member, advisory A3); empty-operation admitted PASS (oracle bound, A3); namespaces third-element PASS (A3); major-1 coercion PASS on the bodies target (it frames only 2.0.0; the unit suite kills it: V3 KILLED ×2).\\n- Oracle defect found (advisory A2): `FuzzNamespaceVocabulary` decides validity with `encoding/json` (last duplicate member wins) while production refuses any duplicate member through the I-JSON gate; the input `{\\\"namespaces\\\":[\\\"credential\\\"],\\\"namespaces\\\":[\\\"blob\\\"]}` makes the target report `valid 2.0.0 namespaces [\\\"blob\\\"] refused: invalid RPC frame` (FAIL, exit 1) although production is right. Reproduced with a one-seed probe target in a scratch clone (`logs/nsvocab-oracle-duplicate-probe-01.log`). A false alarm, not a hole; unreachable at 100x in practice.\\n\\n## (3) Section 17 skew — driven\\n\\nBoth extension directions (`TestExtensionsDirections`); six no-coercion shapes through `Negotiate` with literal `incompatible_protocol`/6; major 1 rejected at every rpcwire entry and both meshneg lanes; my V3 (`major()` coercing 1.0.0 → 2) KILLED ×2 by `TestMajor1RejectedNotReinterpreted`, my M5 (frame 1.0.0 added to the pinned map) KILLED ×2 by `TestMajor1RejectedThroughNegotiation/frame-1.0.0`; error schema not negotiated (RPC 2 refuses 1.3.0, RPC 4/5 refuse 1.0.0, all `ErrVersionMismatch`; bound pairs admit); M6 (v5 exact-array check weakened to a first-element check) KILLED ×2 by `TestPeerOfferRefusals/shape/v5-inexact-rpc`; M7 (`Local` dropped on no-common-major) KILLED ×2 by `TestRefusalShape`.\\n\\n## (4) Replay and lost response\\n\\nMismatched ID/version/nonce-echo/zero expectation classes pinned (`TestResponseCorrelationClasses`); envelope `request_id` correlation-only is an honest bound; operation-key replay adopted from matjournal: byte-identical replay + literal `idempotency_mismatch` at staging (`TestCreateReplayAndConflict`) and at committed (`TestRPCChangedBodyAfterCommitRefusesMismatch`); `Store.Get` returns the true committed phase and a blind identical retry never doubles (`TestRPCBlindRetryAfterCommitNeverDoubles`). Residual (A3): the same two-site narrowing exempting `PhaseRolledBack` (J1b) or `PhaseFailed` (J1c) SURVIVED ×2 — the changed-body rule has no phase qualifier and only the staging and committed members are pinned.\\n\\n## (5) Framing\\n\\n8388608 admitted / 8388609 refused on decode and encode (exact byte counts asserted), embedded LF refused (producer `lf` probe KILLED), valid non-object lines refused, truncated pre-hello frame adopted from `hello_half_frame_close`, unpadded base64url admitted / padded / standard-alphabet refused at the nonce gate (class plants KILLED), `max_object_bytes` independent of `max_line_bytes`. Chunk-data base64url is an honest bound (no chunk validator). My V2 (success envelope admitting an `error` member) KILLED ×2; V4 (body-level object gate skipped for ≤13-byte bodies) SURVIVED ×2 and is an equivalent mutant — the envelope-level `object()` already canonicalizes the whole line, so a nested duplicate member is refused before the body gate runs (this is also why `TestOpaqueBodyMustBeObject/duplicate-member` cannot alone kill the P3-1 probe; the four non-object lanes do).\\n\\n## (6) Story-close items\\n\\nAll green on the exact candidate tree and byte-identical to trunk outside the 20 changed paths (the CR base IS trunk 2fc6d50, so no refresh-carried stale copy is possible; `task-board.config.json` = trunk + 3 rows). `go test ./internal/traceability/...` passes (`TestVerifyRepositoryAcceptsExactOwnership` 140/56 figures, `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry`, `TestREADMEMeasuredCoverageMatchesTracecheckReport`, `TestRunReportsExactCoverageAndFailsClosed`). See (0) for the derivation, ratio, README and LOGBOOK proofs.\\n\\n## (7) Mutation\\n\\n- Producer harnesses re-executed twice each in the isolated extract: rpcwire 43 rows — 41 KILLED by their named tests, `neutral` passed, `error-text` SURVIVED (exit 0 both runs); meshneg 39 rows — 37 KILLED, `neutral` passed, `detail-text` SURVIVED (exit 0 both runs). Identical to the producer's `results.json` for meshneg; the producer's attached rpcwire `results.json` has 42 rows (40 killed) because it predates the two rework probes (A1).\\n- Reviewer harness `review_mutants_rev2.py` (28 rows incl. the 6 inherited-advisory rows, two full runs, per-plant raw `test.log` + overlay + planted source under `reviewer-mutants*/<name>/run{1,2}/`; the package suite runs with no `-run` filter, i.e. unit tests plus fuzz seed corpora, exactly what `go test ./...` executes): 3 harmless controls SURVIVED ×2; 2 equivalents SURVIVED ×2 (R9 rev1 shape, V4); 15 rows KILLED ×2 with the named test failing (main battery: R9b, J1, V1, V2, V3, V5, M5, M6, M7; inherited: N1×4, N2, N3); 8 measurement plants SURVIVED ×2 and recorded as advisory A3 (R9c, J1b, J1c, V6, V7, V8, V9, M4). Of the brief's four shapes: member check dropped (V1, V2 — KILLED), bound widened/moved by one (V5 — KILLED; R8-class widening of the namespace count remains a documented equivalent), unsorted array admitted (first-pair plants KILLED by the producer and rev1 harnesses; third-element plants V6/V7/M4 SURVIVED — A3), pre-mutation revalidation skipped (no such entry exists — stated bound; nearest analogue J1 KILLED, J1b/J1c SURVIVED — A3).\\n\\n## (8) Bounds and hygiene\\n\\ngofmt clean over every `.go` file, `go build ./...`, `go vet ./...`, `cataloggen -adopted … -check`, `GOOS=linux`/`GOOS=windows` builds, JSON census over the 34 non-board `*.json` files, `git diff --check`: all exit 0 (`logs/validation-misc-0{1,2}.log`). No deletions, renames or mode changes in the CR; no `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the evidence tar. `-race -cover` on rpcwire/meshneg/matjournal/hostchannel: ok, no DATA RACE, 99.1 % / 87.8 % / 77.0 % / 84.1 % (`logs/race-scoped-01.log`). The full `-race` run over 38 packages is accepted from the producer's five chunked logs (38 distinct `ok`, zero `DATA RACE`, sessquery 312.889 s) and from the CR construction log, which records the control root's 27 commands green on the exact tree (`required=27 green=27 failed=0 missing=0`; command 5 is the 25 m race gate, command 21 is `cataloggen -adopted -check`).\\n\\nMy own `go test ./... -count=1` on the extract: 37 packages ok, exit 1 because of ONE failure that is not this Story's — see the next section.\\n\\n## Trunk time bomb (out of scope, escalated to the orchestrator)\\n\\n`internal/resumesmoke/support_test.go` hard-codes `smokeDeadline = \\\"2026-09-18T00:00:00.000Z\\\"`; `provhost` wraps each provider call in `context.WithDeadline` on the REAL clock while the smoke's `Now` is a fixed 2026-09-17 clock, so from 2026-09-18T00:00Z on the fake-provider child is cut off before it answers and `TestSmokeThroughRealProviderProcess` fails with `probe call failed: provider_timeout: provider plugin exceeded its deadline: no response before the request deadline`. Proof: fails identically on the trunk extract (2fc6d50) and on the candidate, under a clean `env -i` too; passes (`ok`, 20 s) in a scratch clone with the deadline bumped one day; the file is byte-identical between trunk and candidate and is not among the 20 changed paths. The producer's suite (23:xx UTC) and the CR construction (23:27 UTC) were green because they ran before the deadline. Logs: `logs/test-resumesmoke-{rerun,trunk,cleanenv,liveworktree,diagnostic,deadline-bump}-01.log`. Consequence: every re-run of validation commands 4/5/6 on any tree is red until a trunk fix lands (the same shape as 888ae3d's race-timeout fix); this must be sequenced before the story_final integration.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 29151,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 7288,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
